    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d589">

                <pb facs="0796" n="720" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg720"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5231/1024: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-09-13T18:00:00-04:00">September 13, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>57. Your 58, September 13, 1 p.m. Calderón presented on September 6 a final
                        list<anchor n="19" xml:id="d589-f1"/> of Spanish concessions increasing the
                    automobile quota allotment to 3,363,619 kilograms but refusing all the other
                    American requests of which you were informed in the Department’s telegram No. 51
                    of August 8, 6 p.m.</p>
                <p>The Department has not yet reached a decision but is giving all aspects of the
                    situation the most careful and detailed consideration and is bearing in mind the
                    points brought out by you in your telegram No. 48 of July 18.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
